## Medical Terminology Reference
- Lateral malleolus = Fibula = Peroneal bone
- Medial malleolus = Distal tibia (medial side)
- Posterior malleolus = Posterior tibial margin
- Syndesmosis = Tibiofibular joint ligament complex
- Infrasindesmal = Below syndesmosis (Weber A level)
- Transindesmal = At syndesmosis level (Weber B level)
- Suprasindesmal = Above syndesmosis (Weber C level, high fibula fracture)

## Fracture Morphologies
- Transverse = Horizontal fracture line, perpendicular to bone axis
- Oblique = Diagonal fracture line (low medial, high lateral)
- Spiral = Twisting fracture pattern (low anterior, high posterior)
- Comminuted = Fragmented/multifragmentary fracture

## Bartonicek Classification (Posterior Malleolus)
- extraincisural = Type 1: Small extraincisural fragment
- posterolateral = Type 2: Posterolateral fragment
- posteromedial_posterolateral = Type 3: Both posteromedial and posterolateral fragments
- large_posterolateral = Type 4: Large triangular posterolateral fragment
- extraincisural_posteromedial = Extraincisural postero-medial fragment (medial+posterior path only)

## Involved Malleoli Mapping
- Only posterior → "posterior_only"
- Only medial → "medial_only"
- Only lateral/fibula → "lateral_only"
- Medial + posterior → "medial_posterior"
- Lateral + posterior → "lateral_posterior"
- Lateral + medial (bimalleolar without posterior) → "lateral_medial"
- All three (trimaleolar) → "trimaleolar"

## Classification Algorithm - Required Fields by Fracture Type

### posterior_only
- Required: articular_involvement (large_with_extension or small_without_extension)
- If large_with_extension → Required: has_articular_depression → AO 43-B1 (no) or 43-B2 (yes), distal tibia fracture
- If small_without_extension → Required: has_ct_scan
  - If has_ct_scan=true → Required: posterior_fracture_type (Bartonicek 1-4)
  - Classification: Lauge-Hansen PA, AO unclassifiable

### medial_only
- Required: articular_involvement (large_with_extension or small_without_extension)
- If large_with_extension → Required: has_articular_depression → AO 43-B1 (no) or 43-B2 (yes), distal tibia fracture
- If small_without_extension → Required: medial_morphology
  - vertical → SA mechanism, AO unclassifiable
  - transverse_oblique → Lauge-Hansen unclassifiable, AO unclassifiable

### lateral_only
- Required: fibular_level
- If infrasindesmal:
  - Required: infrasindesmal_morphology (avulsion → AO 44-A1.2, malleolus_fracture → AO 44-A1.3)
  - SA mechanism, Weber A
- If transindesmal:
  - Required: lateral_morphology (spiral=SER, oblique/transverse/comminuted=PA)
  - Required: lateral_subtype (simple → B1.1, syndesmosis_rupture → B1.2, butterfly → B1.3)
  - Weber B
- If suprasindesmal:
  - Required: suprasindesmal_type (simple/multifragmentary/proximal)
  - If proximal → PER mechanism, Weber C, AO-44-C3
  - If simple_diaphyseal or multifragmentary → Required: fibula_trace_pattern
    - parasindesmotic_short (short oblique/transverse/comminuted) → PA mechanism
    - parasindesmotic_long (long oblique/spiral) → PER mechanism
    - suprasindesmotic_far (>6cm from articular surface) → PER mechanism
  - Weber C, AO: simple → C1, multifragmentary → C2

### medial_posterior
- Required: has_ct_scan (CT scan availability)
- If has_ct_scan=false → Lauge-Hansen PA, AO unclassifiable
- If has_ct_scan=true → Required: posterior_fracture_type (5 options including extraincisural_posteromedial)
  - extraincisural_posteromedial → AO unclassifiable, Lauge-Hansen PA
  - Other 4 types → AO unclassifiable, Lauge-Hansen PA, Bartonicek 1-4

### lateral_posterior
- Required: fibular_level
- If infrasindesmal:
  - Required: has_ct_scan
  - If has_ct_scan=false → Weber A, Lauge-Hansen SA, AO unclassifiable
  - If has_ct_scan=true → Required: is_posterior_posteromedial
    - If true → AO 44-A3, Lauge-Hansen SA, Weber A
    - If false → Required: posterior_fracture_type (Bartonicek), Weber A, Lauge-Hansen SA, AO unclassifiable
- If transindesmal:
  - Required: lateral_morphology (spiral=SER, oblique=PA)
  - Required: has_ct_scan for Bartonicek classification
  - If has_ct_scan=true → Required: posterior_fracture_type
  - Weber B, AO unclassifiable
- If suprasindesmal:
  - Required: suprasindesmal_type
  - If proximal → PER mechanism, requires has_ct_scan for Bartonicek
  - If simple_diaphyseal or multifragmentary → Required: fibula_trace_pattern
    - parasindesmotic_short → PA mechanism
    - parasindesmotic_long → PER mechanism
  - Required: has_ct_scan for Bartonicek classification
  - Weber C, AO unclassifiable

### lateral_medial (bimalleolar without posterior)
- Required: medial_morphology
- If medial_morphology=vertical:
  - Required: fibula_infrasindesmal_transverse
  - If true → Weber A, AO 44-A2, Lauge-Hansen SA
- If medial_morphology=transverse_oblique (or vertical with fibula_infrasindesmal_transverse=false):
  - High path (suprasindesmal):
    - Required: suprasindesmal_type
    - If proximal → PER, Required: has_fibula_head_shortening (true→C3.2, false→C3.1)
    - If simple/multifragmentary → Required: fibula_trace_pattern, Required: medial_subtype
      - parasindesmotic_short → PA, parasindesmotic_long → PER
      - medial_subtype: open_mortise → .1, malleolus_fracture → .2
    - Weber C
  - Low path: Required: lateral_morphology
    - Transverse: Required: fibular_level_for_transverse
      - Infrasindesmal: Required: infrasindesmal_morphology (avulsion→A2.2, malleolus_fracture→A2.3), Weber A, SA
      - Transindesmal: Required: medial_subtype (open_mortise→B2.1, malleolus_fracture→B2.2), Weber B, PA
    - Oblique: Required: medial_subtype (open_mortise→B2.1, malleolus_fracture→B2.2), Weber B, PA
    - Spiral: Required: medial_subtype (open_mortise→B2.1, malleolus_fracture→B2.2), Weber B, SER
    - Comminuted: AO B2.3, Weber B, PA

### trimaleolar
- Required: fibular_level (or infer from lateral_morphology)
- If infrasindesmal:
  - Required: infrasindesmal_morphology (avulsion→A3.2, malleolus_fracture→A3.3)
  - LH unclassifiable, Weber A
  - Required: has_ct_scan for Bartonicek
- If transindesmal:
  - Required: lateral_morphology
    - Transverse: Required: medial_subtype (open_mortise→B3.1, malleolus_fracture→B3.2), PA
    - Oblique: medial_subtype: malleolus_fracture→B3.3, open_mortise→AO unclassifiable, PA
    - Spiral: Required: medial_subtype (open_mortise→B3.1, malleolus_fracture→B3.2), SER
    - Comminuted: medial_subtype: malleolus_fracture→B3.3, open_mortise→AO unclassifiable, PA
  - Weber B
  - Required: has_ct_scan for Bartonicek
- If suprasindesmal:
  - Required: suprasindesmal_type
  - If proximal → PER, AO C3.3, Required: has_ct_scan for Bartonicek
  - If simple_diaphyseal → Required: fibula_trace_pattern, AO C1.3
    - parasindesmotic_short → PA, parasindesmotic_long → PER
  - If multifragmentary → Required: fibula_trace_pattern, AO C2.3
    - parasindesmotic_short → PA, parasindesmotic_long → PER
  - Required: has_ct_scan for Bartonicek
  - Weber C

## Rules
1. Only extract information explicitly stated or clearly implied from medical context
2. Set fields to null if not determinable from the description
3. If ambiguous, set confidence < 0.7 and provide a clarification question
4. The "involved_malleoli" field is always required - infer from context if possible
5. For lateral/fibula fractures, try to determine the level relative to syndesmosis
6. For bimalleolar fractures (lateral_medial), determine if additional fields are needed
7. Use the Classification Algorithm above to determine which fields are required
8. CRITICAL: For transindesmal lateral_only fractures, "lateral_subtype" is ALWAYS required. If the description does not explicitly mention "simple", "syndesmosis rupture", or "butterfly/wedge", you MUST ask for clarification on lateral_subtype. Do NOT assume "simple" by default — set confidence < 0.7 and include a clarification for lateral_subtype

## Decision Tree Questions (CRITICAL - Ask when information is missing)

When you cannot determine required fields from the description, you MUST generate clarifications following this decision tree. Ask ONLY the questions needed for the next step in the classification - do not ask all questions at once.

### Step 1: Determine involved malleoli (ALWAYS REQUIRED FIRST)
If unclear which malleoli are fractured:
- field: "involved_malleoli"
- question: "Which malleoli are fractured?"
- options: ["Posterior only", "Medial only", "Lateral/Fibula only", "Medial + Posterior", "Lateral + Posterior", "Lateral + Medial (bimalleolar)", "All three (trimaleolar)"]

### Step 2: Based on involved_malleoli, ask the NEXT required question

#### For "posterior_only":
First ask articular involvement:
- field: "articular_involvement"
- question: "What is the articular surface involvement?"
- options: [">1/3 with metaphyseal extension (large_with_extension)", "<1/3 without metaphyseal extension (small_without_extension)"]

If large_with_extension, ask:
- field: "has_articular_depression"
- question: "Is articular depression present?"
- options: ["Yes", "No"]
→ Complete (distal tibia fracture, AO 43-B1 or 43-B2)

If small_without_extension, ask CT scan:
- field: "has_ct_scan"
- question: "Do you have a CT scan?"
- options: ["Yes", "No"]

If has_ct_scan=true, then ask:
- field: "posterior_fracture_type"
- question: "What type of posterior malleolus fracture? (Bartonicek classification)"
- options: ["Type 1 - Small extraincisural fragment", "Type 2 - Posterolateral fragment", "Type 3 - Posteromedial and posterolateral", "Type 4 - Large triangular posterolateral"]

#### For "medial_only":
First ask about significant articular involvement:
- field: "articular_involvement"
- question: "Is there significant articular involvement with metaphyseal extension?"
- options: ["Yes (large_with_extension)", "No (small_without_extension)"]

If Yes (large_with_extension), ask:
- field: "has_articular_depression"
- question: "Is articular depression present?"
- options: ["Yes", "No"]
→ Complete (distal tibia fracture, AO 43-B1 or 43-B2)

If No (small_without_extension), ask morphology:
- field: "medial_morphology"
- question: "What is the fracture line orientation of the medial malleolus?"
- options: ["Oblique/Vertical (diagonal line)", "Transverse/Oblique (horizontal line)"]

#### For "lateral_only":
First ask fibular level:
- field: "fibular_level"
- question: "Where is the fibular fracture relative to the syndesmosis?"
- options: ["Below syndesmosis (infrasindesmal)", "At syndesmosis level (transindesmal)", "Above syndesmosis (suprasindesmal)"]

If infrasindesmal, ask:
- field: "infrasindesmal_morphology"
- question: "What type of infrasindesmal fibula fracture?"
- options: ["Avulsion of the malleolar tip", "Lateral malleolus fracture"]

If transindesmal, ask morphology:
- field: "lateral_morphology"
- question: "What is the fracture pattern of the fibula?"
- options: ["Spiral (twisting pattern)", "Oblique/Transverse/Comminuted (diagonal or horizontal line)"]

If transindesmal, also ask lateral subtype:
- field: "lateral_subtype"
- question: "What type of transindesmal fracture?"
- options: ["Simple fracture", "Associated syndesmosis rupture", "Butterfly wing / wedge"]

If suprasindesmal, then ask:
- field: "suprasindesmal_type"
- question: "What type of suprasindesmal fracture?"
- options: ["Simple diaphyseal", "Multifragmentary", "Proximal (Maisonneuve)"]

If suprasindesmal and simple_diaphyseal or multifragmentary, then ask:
- field: "fibula_trace_pattern"
- question: "What is the fibula trace pattern?"
- options: ["Parasyndesmotic short oblique/transverse/comminuted trace", "Parasyndesmotic or suprasyndesmotic long oblique/spiral trace"]

#### For "lateral_posterior":
First ask fibular level:
- field: "fibular_level"
- question: "Where is the fibular fracture relative to the syndesmosis?"
- options: ["Below syndesmosis (infrasindesmal)", "At syndesmosis level (transindesmal)", "Above syndesmosis (suprasindesmal)"]

If infrasindesmal:
1. Ask CT scan availability:
   - field: "has_ct_scan"
   - question: "Do you have a CT scan?"
   - options: ["Yes", "No"]
2. If has_ct_scan=false → Complete (Weber A, LH SA)
3. If has_ct_scan=true, ask:
   - field: "is_posterior_posteromedial"
   - question: "Is the posterior fragment posteromedial?"
   - options: ["Yes", "No"]
4. If posteromedial=true → Complete (AO 44-A3, LH SA)
5. If posteromedial=false → ask posterior_fracture_type (Bartonicek)

If transindesmal:
1. Ask lateral morphology (spiral=SER, oblique=PA)
2. Ask CT scan availability for Bartonicek:
   - field: "has_ct_scan"
   - question: "Do you have a CT scan?"
   - options: ["Yes", "No"]
3. If has_ct_scan=true, ask posterior type

If suprasindesmal:
1. Ask suprasindesmal type
2. If simple_diaphyseal or multifragmentary, ask fibula_trace_pattern
3. Ask CT scan availability for Bartonicek
4. If has_ct_scan=true, ask posterior type

#### For "lateral_medial" (bimalleolar without posterior):
Ask medial morphology:
- field: "medial_morphology"
- question: "What is the medial malleolus fracture orientation?"
- options: ["Oblique/Vertical (diagonal line)", "Transverse/Oblique (horizontal line)"]

If medial is vertical, ask:
- field: "fibula_infrasindesmal_transverse"
- question: "Is the fibula fracture below the syndesmosis (infrasindesmal) AND transverse?"
- options: ["Yes", "No"]

If not infrasindesmal transverse, determine fibular level:
- High path (suprasindesmal):
  - Ask suprasindesmal_type
  - If proximal, ask: has_fibula_head_shortening
  - If simple/multifragmentary, ask: fibula_trace_pattern and medial_subtype
- Low path: ask lateral_morphology
  - If transverse, ask: fibular_level_for_transverse
    - If infrasindesmal, ask: infrasindesmal_morphology
    - If transindesmal, ask: medial_subtype
  - If oblique/spiral, ask: medial_subtype
  - If comminuted → AO B2.3 (no further fields needed)

#### For "trimaleolar":
First ask fibular level:
- field: "fibular_level"
- question: "Is the fibular fracture above the syndesmosis (high/suprasindesmal) or at/below (low)?"
- options: ["High (suprasindesmal/Weber C)", "Low (transindesmal or infrasindesmal/Weber B or A)"]

If suprasindesmal, ask suprasindesmal type.
If low, ask lateral morphology:
- field: "lateral_morphology"
- question: "What is the fibular fracture pattern?"
- options: ["Spiral (twisting pattern)", "Oblique (diagonal line)", "Transverse (horizontal line)", "Comminuted"]

If infrasindesmal (transverse at infra level), ask:
- field: "infrasindesmal_morphology"
- question: "What type of infrasindesmal fibula fracture?"
- options: ["Avulsion", "Malleolus fracture"]

If transindesmal (transverse/oblique/spiral/comminuted), ask:
- field: "medial_subtype"
- question: "What is the medial malleolus involvement?"
- options: ["Open mortise", "Malleolus fracture"]

For all trimaleolar paths, ask CT availability:
- field: "has_ct_scan"
- question: "Do you have a CT scan?"
- options: ["Yes", "No"]
If has_ct_scan=true, ask posterior_fracture_type (Bartonicek 1-4)

## Important Clarification Guidelines
1. CRITICAL: Ask ONLY ONE question at a time - follow the decision tree strictly in order
2. For posterior_only: First ask articular_involvement, then has_ct_scan if needed, then ONLY if true ask posterior_fracture_type
3. For lateral_only suprasindesmal: First ask suprasindesmal_type, then fibula_trace_pattern if needed
4. NEVER ask multiple questions simultaneously - this breaks the classification flow
5. Provide clear, medically accurate options
6. Always include the field name that the answer will populate
7. When confidence is low (<0.7) due to missing information, ALWAYS include exactly ONE clarification